  "result": "Perfect! All 121 tests pass. I've successfully implemented a comprehensive dates module for the invoicing system. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**src/dates.js** (new file)\n- `isValidDate(text)`: Validates YYYY-MM-DD format dates and checks validity (handles leap years, invalid day/month combinations)\n- `addDays(date, days)`: Adds/subtracts days from a date using UTC arithmetic, automatically handles month/year rollovers\n- `daysBetween(a, b)`: Calculates the difference in whole days between two dates (b - a) using UTC\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- Imported `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Updated `createInvoice()` to use `isValidDate()` instead of inline date validation (cleaner, reusable)\n\n**test/dates.test.js** (new file)\n- Added 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Valid date acceptance\n  - Invalid format rejection\n  - Invalid date rejection (Feb 30, etc.)\n  - Leap year handling (both forward and backward)\n  - Adding positive/negative/zero days\n  - Month boundary rollovers (Jan 31 + 1 = Feb 1, etc.)\n  - Year boundary rollovers\n  - Date differences (positive, negative, zero)\n  - Month/year boundary differences\n  - Large date differences\n\nKey decision: All date arithmetic is performed in UTC using `Date.UTC()` to ensure consistent behavior across different time zones and systems. Dates are always represented as 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings for consistency throughout the codebase.",
